<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bhillama V</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1173–<a href="/years/1192">1192</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bhillama V was a Seuna <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yadava">Yadava</a> ruler who reigned from about 1173 to 1192 and made his dynasty an independent power. Exploiting the collapse of the Western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalukya-dynasty">Chalukyas</a>, he seized Kalyani and the northern Chalukya provinces around 1187 and founded Devagiri (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daulatabad">Daulatabad</a>) as his capital. His advance south was halted by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoysala-empire">Hoysala</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/veera-ballala-ii">Veera Ballala II</a>, who defeated him in 1190.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bhillama-v.jpg" alt="Bhillama V" width="320" height="149" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG Coins · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yadavas_of_Devagiri._Bhillama_V._1185-1193.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
